{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule5EventP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event reader is a collection of the new events, oldest first. Each system type has its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place in the events, so it sees each event once however many other systems read them too. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"following system applies each "},{"code":"Damage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" event to the health of its target:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct ApplyDamage {","    func run(_ damages: EventReader<Damage>, _ health: Update<Health>) {","        health { health, entity in","            for damage in damages where damage.target == entity {","                health.current -= damage.amount","            }","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Health(current: 30))","world.send(Damage(target: knight, amount: 12))","Schedule { ApplyDamage() }.run(on: &world)","print(world[Health.self, of: knight].current)","\/\/ Prints \"18\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world keeps an event for the rest of the update it was sent in and all of the next; see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A system that doesn’t run for longer than that misses the events dropped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7Systems11EventReaderV","title":"EventReader","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventReader"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SystemParameters.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/SystemParameters.swift#L236"}},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/endIndex","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/events","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/startIndex"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/subscript(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Subscripts","anchor":"Subscripts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/BidirectionalCollection-Implementations","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/Collection-Implementations","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/RandomAccessCollection-Implementations","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader\/Sequence-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshi